#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The Idiograph merge gate and its commit command. One script, one machine-readable verdict.

Copied from the gate of the repository Idiograph was split from (20 October 2026). The app is
this repo's root and its suite is tests/. The real study data the suite's reference checks read,
the names the scans look for and the real-name scan's script live only on the maintainer's Mac,
named in the local gate file (GATE_LOCAL below). Without it those checks skip and say so.

USAGE

    ./verify --fast     seconds, no gate: document budgets, the pseudonym scan, the
                        case-folder-name scan, the conflict markers and the
                        participants'-words scan from its cache
    ./verify --docs     adds the banned-pattern report, and proves the diff is docs only
    ./verify            the full gate: everything, plus py_compile, the gate's own
                        tests, the real-name scan, the participants'-words scan
                        reading the case data when it changed, and the Idiograph suite
    ./commit -m "<message>" -- <path>...
                        commits exactly the named paths, nothing else staged or not
                        (./commit runs ./verify --commit)

READ THE LAST LINE OF STDOUT, NEVER THE EXIT CODE.

    VERIFY: GREEN merge=yes mode=full sha=<sha> tree=clean snap=<tree sha>
    VERIFY: RED merge=no mode=full sha=<sha> tree=dirty reason=budgets snap=<tree sha>
    COMMIT: GREEN sha=<new sha>
    COMMIT: RED reason=<slug>

`merge=yes` appears only on GREEN. This repo has no branches and no remote, so
it means safe to commit, nothing more. `tree=clean` reports whether
`git status --porcelain` is empty and is informational: Adam's working tree
carries unrelated edits most of the time, and that is not a failure.

THE SNAPSHOT. Every run checks a frozen copy, never the tree itself. It clones
every tracked file and every untracked unignored one (APFS clonefile, so no bytes
are copied) into $IDIOGRAPH_VERIFY_TMP/idiograph-verify-snap-<pid>/, freezes a copy
of the index beside it, and hashes the copy into a git tree object through a
temporary index. That tree is `snap=` on the verdict, so a commit can be checked
against what passed. An edit or a commit in the real tree mid-run changes nothing
that is checked. The copy is removed at the end, whatever the verdict. The real
study data is outside the repository, so the name scan and the Idiograph suite
read the real folders, never writing to them.

TWO LOCKS, both in $IDIOGRAPH_VERIFY_TMP (default /tmp). The run lock,
idiograph-verify-run.lock, is held for the whole run, so a second run refuses
with reason=locked. The commit lock, idiograph-verify.lock, is held by a run only
while it takes its snapshot, and by ./commit while it checks and commits, so a
commit waits seconds for a run, never minutes.

THE SHARED MAC. A full run shares Adam's Mac by the rule in
~/.claude/coordinator-principles.md, "Sharing one Mac between fleets", as
~/.claude/bin/heavy does. Before it takes any lock, it waits as
~/.claude/machine-load/waiting/academy-<pid>.json. While a Harbour gate heads
Harbour's queue, it waits with no time limit. Harbour marks its head
"queueHead": true in waiting/, and once any live Harbour waiter carries the field,
the flag alone decides. Until then Harbour's head is its earliest live waiter by
enqueuedAt (else the id's leading milliseconds, else the file's time), in
waiting/ or in Harbour's own queue folder, where an entry with no project is
Harbour's. Otherwise it waits while another project has a waiter that queued
before it and has waited over 20 minutes, or while its own place would make more
than the machine's two, each live announced run counting its "places" (1 when
absent, 2 for Harbour's full gate), at most 60 minutes in all. A file counts only
while its pid lives and that process started no later than a minute after the
file's own time, so a reused pid counts for nothing. It then takes the run lock
(refusing locked as ever, its waiter file gone) and is announced, "places": 1, as
~/.claude/machine-load/academy-<pid>.json until it ends. Both go however it
ends. A run started inside another announced run, as when heavy runs ./verify,
has its place already, so it neither waits nor is announced again. --fast, --docs
and ./commit take no place, never wait, and run or commit while a full run waits.
HEAVY_NO_WAIT=1 skips the wait, and HEAVY_QUEUES names the queue folders as it
does for heavy. IDIOGRAPH_MACHINE_LOAD names another machine-load folder,
IDIOGRAPH_MACHINE_QUEUES its queue folders, IDIOGRAPH_MACHINE_CAP another cap in
seconds and IDIOGRAPH_MACHINE_OLD another 20 minutes in seconds, for the gate's own
tests. With IDIOGRAPH_VERIFY_TMP set and no IDIOGRAPH_MACHINE_LOAD, or on a machine
with neither heavy nor the folder, a run neither waits nor is announced, and says
so in one line.

./commit takes the commit lock, waiting up to three minutes, runs the fast
checks on the tree as it will stand (HEAD plus the named paths), and commits
exactly the named paths. When it changes code (.py, .js, verify, commit, anything
under tests/ or Tools/idiograph/) it also needs a GREEN full verdict in
.verify/history.log whose snap holds that code's present content.

THE RULE BOTH SESSIONS FOLLOW: commit only through ./commit, never a bare git
commit, and land code on a GREEN full gate, the train's. No warning to the other
session is needed before a full gate.

THE FULL GATE IS THE COORDINATOR'S TRAIN, about four a day and one before the
hand-over (Adam, 18 October). A build finishes with its targeted check instead,
once, at the end: Tools/idiograph/tests/test_idiograph.py --changed, or --area.
The gate sets IDIOGRAPH_TRAIN=1 for the Idiograph suite, which runs every area in
a train alone and skips itself anywhere else, and a suite that skipped itself
here is RED with reason=idiograph-not-run. The coordinator runs the train in the
background:

    ./verify > .verify/last.log 2>&1 &
    until grep -q '^VERIFY:' .verify/last.log; do sleep 10; done; tail -1 .verify/last.log

Never block inside a tool call for longer than the prompt cache lives. Diagnose
a red before re-running it.

iCloud keeps the older side of a clash between its upload and a local write as
"<name> 2.<ext>" beside the file. Such a copy is never part of the snapshot. A
copy byte for byte the same as its file at HEAD, in the index or on disk is
moved to .verify/icloud-copies/ at the start of a run. A copy that differs is
left where it is and named, since it may hold work.

Every verdict is appended to .verify/history.log.
"""

